{
  "_id": "dHGoioVqeEAFUj6n",
  "name": "Illusory Dragon",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-breath-purple.webp",
  "folder": "yXi4rP3BbtNBsPwp",
  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Gathering threads of shadow from the Shadowfell, you create a Huge shadowy dragon in an unoccupied space you can see within range. The illusion lasts for the duration and occupies its space as if it were a creature. The shadow material makes it tangible, but it has Immunity to all damage and conditions.</p><p>When the illusion appears, each enemy that can see it makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, the creature drops whatever it is holding and has the &amp;Reference[frightened apply=false]{Frightened} condition for the duration. If a creature Frightened this way ends its turn in a space without line of sight to the illusion, it repeats the save, ending the condition on itself on a success.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can move the illusion up to 60 feet. At any point during this movement, you can have it exhale a blast of energy in a 60-foot Cone. Each creature in the Cone makes an Intelligence saving throw, taking 6d6 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Necrotic, or Poison damage (your choice when you create the dragon) on a failure or half as much on a success.</p><p>A creature that takes a Study action to examine the dragon can recognize it as an illusion with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. A creature that discerns the illusion can see through it and has Advantage on saving throws to end the Frightened condition it caused and against its exhalation.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
